o. HIV and AIDS Prevention and Control - refers to measures aimed at protecting non-infected persons from contracting HIV and minimizing the impact of the condition of persons living with HIV;

p. HIV and STI Counseling - refers to the provision of information on STTI, HIV and AIDS, how it is spread and how it may be prevented, risk-reduction approaches, and information on treatment, care and support for persons living with HIV, which is conducted before and after HIV testing;

q. HIV Testing - refers to any facility-based or mobile medical procedure that is conducted to determine the presence or absence of HIV in person's body;

r. Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) - refers to the virus that destroys the immune system of a person which causes AIDS;

s. Indigent Clients - refers to clients that fit to the criteria and definition of the Davao City Social Services and Development Office;

t. Information Material - shall mean any written and/or printed material which educates the public;

u. Key Populations at Higher Risk of STTI and HIV Exposure or "Key Populations" - refer to those persons whose behavior make them more likely to be exposed to HIV or to transmit the virus, as determined by Philippine National AIDS Council (PNAC);

v. Medical Confidentiality - refers to the relationship of trust and confidence created or existing between a patient or a person living with HIV and his or her attending health care providers and or any person providing services or those who have access to medical records;

w. Medical Practitioner - licensed Doctor of Medicine engaged in health work in hospitals, clinics, sanitaria, health stations, barangay health centers and the like;

x. Partner Notification - refers to the method of finding and counseling the sexual partner(s) of a person who has been diagnosed as having Sexually-Transmitted Infection and HIV;

y. Peer Educator - is a trained STTI, HIV and AIDS educator who is capable of influencing, motivating and developing healthy behaviors among his/her peers;

z. Person Living with HIV - refers to any individual diagnosed to be infected with HIV;

aa. Quality Healthcare - as indicated by standards set by WHO, accessibility and affordability of medical needs, ethical care, and appropriateness of provider's knowledge on STTI, HIV and AIDS, sexual and reproductive health and rights, gender sensitive in their interpersonal relations with patients and adopt diagnostic treatment and follow up procedure of health providers;

bb. Reproductive Health - it is a state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease or infirmity in all matters relating to the reproductive system and its functions and processes, as defined in the Cairo International Conference on Population and Development, and World Health Organization adopted the International Conference on Population and Development;

cc. Reproductive Health and Wellness Center (RHWC) - it's a wellness center which purpose is to achieve universal availability and accessibility of reproductive health care and services, provides HIV related services and treatment in Davao City;

dd. Health Education, Promotion and Development Division - Conducts information, education and promotion campaign and training on Reproductive Health, STTI, HIV and AIDS activities under the City Health Office;

