**ARTICLE VI - ADMINISTRATION AND OPERATION**

**SECTION 1. ADMINISTRATION -** The administration of the City College of Davao shall be vested in the President who shall render full-time service. The powers and duties of the President, in addition to those specifically provided under existing and prevailing CHEd Memorandum Order(s) (M.O.), shall be those usually pertaining to the Offices of the President of other colleges/universities, and those delegated by the Board of Trustees.

**ARTICLE VII - SEARCH COMMITTEE FOR THE PRESIDENT, SEARCH PROCESS, MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS, AND VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT**

**SECTION 1. CONSTITUTION OF SEARCH COMMITTEE -** Within six (6) months before the expiration of the term of office of the incumbent President, the Board of Trustees shall constitute a Search Committee for President (SCP) which shall consist of representatives from the Academe, the Private Sector, the Civil Service Commission (CSC), the Commission on Higher Education (CHEd), the Association of Local Colleges and Universities (ALCU), the City Administrator of Davao, and other relevant government agencies as may be identified by the BOT. The SCP shall designate the Chairperson of the SCP from among the members of the SCP. The SCP shall meet within fifteen (15) days from its constitution.

Qualifications of SCP members shall be in accordance with the existing guidelines of the CHEd.

**SECTION 2. FUNDS -** The Board of Trustees shall appropriate adequate funds to finance the activities of the Search Committee for President.

**SECTION 3. VACANCY, PROCEDURE FOR THE SEARCH AND MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS -** The Search Committee for President (SCP) shall be guided by the search process and minimum qualifications set by the Commission on Higher Education (CHEd).

**ARTICLE VIII - TERM OF OFFICE, POWERS AND DUTIES OF THE PRESIDENT**

**SECTION 1. TERM OF OFFICE -** The President shall be selected and appointed by the Governing Board for a term of four (4) years and shall be eligible for reappointment for another term only.

**SECTION 2. POWERS AND DUTIES -** The administration and supervision of the CCO is vested in the President who must render full time service. He shall be responsible to the Board for the implementation of all its programs, projects, and services.

**SECTION 3. APPOINTMENT OF OFFICIALS -** The President shall appoint the Vice-President, Secretary of the College, Program Heads, Directors, Registrar, Administrative Officer, Accountant, teaching and non-teaching personnel subject to the confirmation of the Board; provided that the President for Academic Affairs must be a holder of an earned doctoral degree; provided further that their appointments shall be pursuant to existing Civil Service laws, rules, and regulations.

**ARTICLE IX - FACULTY AND NON-TEACHING PERSONNEL**

**SECTION 1. COMPOSITION -** The Faculty of the City College of Davao (CCD) shall be composed of Program Heads, Professors, Instructors, Regular Lecturers, or the Teaching Personnel of CCD. The Vice- Presidents, Program Heads who shall be the heads of the various colleges, Registrar, Administrative Officer, Accountants, non-teaching personnel and other officials shall be appointed by the President subject to the confirmation of the Board; provided further that their appointments shall be pursuant to existing Civil Service laws, rules, and regulations.

