ss. Person Living with HIV (PLHIV) refers to any individual diagnosed to be infected with HIV;
tt. Pre-exposure Prophylaxis refers to the use of prescription drugs as a strategy for the prevention of HIV infection by people who do not have the HIV and AIDS. It is an optional treatment, which may be taken by people who are HIV-negative but who have substantial, higher-than-average risk of contracting an HIV infection;
uu. Pre-test Counseling refers to the process of providing an individual with information on the biomedical aspects of HIV, AIDS, and emotional support to any psychological implications of undergoing HIV testing and the test result itself before the individual is subjected to the test;
vv. Post-exposure Prophylaxis refers to a preventive medical treatment started immediately after exposure to pathogen (HIV) in order to prevent infection by the pathogen and the development of the disease;
ww. Post-test Counseling refers to the process of providing risk-reduction information and emotional support to a person who submitted to HIV testing at the time the result is released;
xx. Prophylactic refers to any agent or device used to prevent the transmission of an infection;
yy. Provider-initiated Counseling and Testing refers to a health care provider initiating HIV testing to a person practicing high-risk behavior or vulnerable to HIV after conducting HIV pre-test counseling. A person may elect to decline or defer testing such that consent is conditional;
zz. Quality Health Care - as indicated in the standards set by the World Health Organization (WHO), accessibility and affordability of medical needs, ethical care, and appropriateness of provider's knowledge on STI, HIV and AIDS, sexual and reproductive health rights, gender sensitivity in their interpersonal relations with patients and adopt diagnostic treatment and follow-up procedure of health providers;
aaa. Redress refers to an act of compensation for unfairness, grievance, and reparation;
bbb. Reproductive Health - It is a state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease and infirmity in all matters relating to the reproductive system and its functions and processes. It implies that people are able to have satisfying and safe sex lives and they have the capability to reproduce and freedom to decide if, when, and how often to do so as defined in the Cairo International Conference on Population and Development (CICPD) and World Health Organization (WHO);
ccc. Reproductive Health and Wellness Center (RHWC) - A primary healthcare facility under the local government of the City of Davao that serves at the forefront of STI, HIV and AIDS prevention, treatment, care and support. Its purpose is to achieve universal availability, affordability, accessibility of reproductive health care services;

--- [Page 8] ---
Page 8 of 24
Ord. No. 0707-24

ddd. Safer Sex Practices refer to choices made and behaviors adopted by a person to reduce or minimize the risk of HIV transmission. This may include postponing sexual debut, non-penetrative sex, correct and consistent use of male or female condoms, and reducing the number of sexual partners;

eee. Sexual Health implies that the sexual drive and sexual processes are accomplished in a state of complete physical, mental, and social being, not merely the absence of disease or disorder;

fff. Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs) refer to infections that are spread through the transfer of organisms from one person to another as a result of sexual contact;

ggg. Sexual Orientation refers to the direction of emotional, sexual attraction, conduct towards people of the same sex (homosexual orientation) or towards people of both sexes (bisexual orientation) or towards people of the opposite sex (heterosexual orientation) or to the absence of sexual attraction (asexual orientation);

hhh. Social Protection refers to a set of policies and programs designed to reduce poverty and vulnerability by promoting efficient labor markets, diminishing people's exposure to risks, and enhancing their capacity to protect themselves against hazards, and interruptions on, or loss of income;

iii. Standard Precautions refer to work practices required to reduce the risk of transmission of blood-borne and other pathogens from both recognized and unrecognized sources to protect the health care worker and client;

jjj. STI, HIV and AIDS Workplace Policies refer to the statement of provisions of work and health benefits and rights for workers/employees;

kkk. Stigma refers to the dynamic devaluation and dehumanization of an individual in the eyes of others, which may be based on attributes that are arbitrarily defined by others as discreditable or unworthy, and which results in discrimination when acted upon;

III. Treatment hubs refer to private and public hospitals or medical establishments accredited by DOH to have the capacity and facility to provide treatment and care services to PLHIV;

mmm. Voluntary HIV testing refers to HIV testing done on an individual who, after having undergone pre-test counseling, willingly submits to such test;

nnn. Vulnerable Communities refer to the communities and groups suffering from vulnerabilities, such as unequal opportunities, social exclusion, poverty, unemployment, and other similar social, economic, cultural, and political conditions making them more susceptible to STI, HIV and AIDS; (RA 11166)

ooo. Workplace refers to the office premises and work site where workers are habitually employed and shall include the office or place where workers, with no fixed or definite work site, regularly report for assignment in the course of their employment;

--- [Page 9] ---
Page 9 of 24
Ord. No. 0707-24

Article IV. The Davao City AIDS Council (DCAC), the DCAC Secretariat, and the City Health Office - Reproductive Health and Wellness Center

a. Lead in ensuring and coordinating the crafting, operationalization, and implementation of the City's strategic, medium-term, operational, investment, and other plans, programs, and policies related to STI, HIV, and AIDS;

b. Recommend measures to the Local Health Board (LHB), City Development Council, City Mayor, and Sangguniang Panlungsod in adopting, formulating, developing, reviewing, and updating of policies, plans, or programs towards achieving the City's STI, HIV, and AIDS targets;

c. Oversee the coordination and undertaking of STI, HIV, and AIDS prevention programs, including information, education, and communication; research; provision of screening, testing, and counselling; as well as ensuring provision of health and other support services;

d. Lead the monitoring, assessment, and evaluation of the operationalization and implementation of the operationalization and the policies, plans, and programs relative thereto; the City's implementation of its mandates as set in the national policies and international commitments including the Philippine HIV and AIDS Policy Act, the AIDS Medium Term Plan, among others, and/or compliance, operationalization, and/or actions of local bodies with this Council's policies, resolutions, and recommendations;

e. Coordinate the establishment, mobilization, and strengthening of local, national and international linkages with stakeholders involved in STI, HIV, and AIDS response;

f. By itself, through its Chairperson or any of its authorized members, partner, or engage with, or secure assistance or services of public, private, non-government/civil society organizations in pursuit of its mandates, subject to existing laws and regulations;

g. Consistent with the structure provided in this Ordinance, adopt its operational and functional structure, form committees and subcommittees, working groups, define respective roles and responsibilities in furtherance of its mandates;

h. Oversee the reconstitution of the DCAC Secretariat, its staffing pattern, and its operations, through its Chairperson, or its duly authorized Officer or Member;

i. Propose budget for its operations and that of its Secretariat;

--- [Page 10] ---
Page 10 of 24
Ord. No. 0707-24

j. Adopt its own rules, resolutions, and recommendations in furtherance of the above powers and functions.

Sufficient personnel shall be assigned and constituted as Secretariat of the DCAC and shall perform the following functions:
1. Assist and provide technical and administrative support to the DCAC, its Chair, its Members, and the respective leads of Committees, Sub-Committees or Working Groups in the performance of their functions;
2. Serve as the communication center of the DCAC;
3. Serve as custodian of records and repository of all data and information pertaining to the City's response to STI, HIV, and AIDS, the DCAC, and the DCAC operations – including meetings, activities, programs, projects, among others; and
4. Perform other secretarial functions as may be assigned by the Chairperson of the Council or authorized officers;

