**Article VII. STI, HIV AND AIDS Treatment, Psychosocial Care and Support**

**SECTION 1. PSYCHOSOCIAL CARE AND SUPPORT TO PERSONS LIVING WITH HIV AND AFFECTED FAMILIES: The City Government of Davao, through the CHO-RHMM, treatment hubs and other HIV support groups, shall ensure availability, affordability, accessibility, and treatment of STI and HIV to Persons Living with HIV and provide education on adherence to treatment. The CSWDQ, in coordination with DSWD and other service providers, shall provide psychosocial care and support programs to PLHIV and affected families.**

**SECTION 2. CARE AND SUPPORT FOR OVERSEAS WORKERS LIVING WITH HIV: The CSWDQ, in coordination with OWWA, DMW, DOH, CHO, DSWD, and CSOs, shall develop a stigma-free comprehensive reintegration, care, and support program including economic, social, and medical support for overseas workers who have been repatriated or are about to be repatriated due to their HIV positive status.**

**SECTION 3. SPECIAL CARE AND SUPPORT SERVICES FOR PREGNANT WOMEN WITH STI, HIV AND AIDS: The CHO, through its Mental Health Programs in coordination with CSDWO and other accredited agencies/institutions shall provide special care and support services for pregnant women with STI, HIV and AIDS and shall be integrated in the development plans and activities of the department.**

**SECTION 4. SPECIAL CARE AND SUPPORT SERVICES FOR CHILDREN INFECTED WITH HIV AND CHILDREN OF PERSONS LIVING WITH HIV AND AIDS: Treatment hubs, in coordination with CSDWO and other accredited institutions, shall provide psychosocial care and other interventions at the best interest of the child.**

