**CHAPTER XXXI. ESTABLISHMENT OF INDUSTRIES, PROJECTS, PLANTS, FACILITIES AND UNDERTAKINGS WHICH MAY CREATE OR PRODUCE ENVIRONMENTAL HEALTH POLLUTION HAZARDS OR IMPACTS**

**SECTION I. The provisions of this Chapter shall apply to all establishments, industries, projects, plants, facilities, and premises which may create or produce environmental health pollution hazards or impacts or which raw materials used, by products, end-products, or by products' waste products and other processes, activities or undertakings may generate pollution hazards or impacts on workers and the communities exposed such as, but not limited to the following:**

a. Health care institutions and facilities;

b. Establishments engaged in transport industries;

c. Establishments engaged in construction activities;

d. Establishments engaged in the manufacture, storage and/or use of fertilizers and pesticides;

e. Establishments engaged in the manufacture and processing of papers, cellulose, wood and wood products;

f. Establishments engaged in the milling of corn, rice, feeds and flours and other food materials and additives;

g. Establishments engaged in the processing and manufacture of cement/fiber glass/boards;

h. Sawn timber yards;

i. Automotive and car assembling/manufacturing plants;

j. Establishments using biomass as fuels;

k. Establishments engaged in the processing, smelting and manufacture of steel products;

l. Shops and cottage industries;

m. Establishments engaged in the processing, storage and manufacture of firecrackers, explosives, and ammunition;

n. Establishments engaged in the manufacture of electric installations and power generation;

o. Establishments engaged in the manufacture and sale of electric and electronic products;

p. Establishments engaged in the bulk storage, processing and/or sale of gasoline, gas and other petro-chemical products;

q. Establishments engaged in the processing and manufacture of batteries, laboratory chemicals, cosmetics, and pharmaceuticals;

r. Establishments engaged in the manufacturing, cleaning, storing and/or selling activities;

s. Sanitary landfills and other garbage disposal sites;

t. Sludge, gravel and sand extraction, grinding, and filling activities, facilities or balancing plants;

u. Establishments engaged in the drilling or boring of underground water sources;

v. Establishments engaged in the mining of cement and other aggregates and prefabricated products;

w. Establishments engaged in the manufacture and processing of industrial and medical gases;

x. Other projects, activities, operations, and undertakings that would create or produce environmental health hazards and impacts.

