**ARTICLE IV**

**PARTICIPATION**

**Section 5. Office for Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA).** The Office for Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA) is hereby strengthened to ensure the integration and participation of Older Persons in the formulation and implementation of policies directly affecting their well-being.

**Section 6. Chairperson of the Office for Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA).** The OSCA shall be chaired by a senior citizen who shall be appointed by the City Mayor for a term of three (3) years without reappointment from a list of three (3) nominees submitted by the Sangguniang Panlungsod through a resolution;

The Chairperson shall be assisted by the City Social Services Development Office (CSSDO) in coordination with the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD). He/She shall be entitled to receive an honorarium in the amount at least equivalent to Salary Grade 22;

**Section 7. Selection Procedure of the Nominees for the position of Chairperson of the Office for Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA).** The following procedure shall be complied with in the selection of the nominees for the position of Chairperson of the Office for Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA):

a) The nominees for the OSCA Chairperson shall be chosen/recommended in a general assembly by and among the members of the various Senior Citizen's Chapter Organizations in the City of Davao duly registered with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) or Cooperative Development Authority (CDA) and the City Social Services Development Office (CSSDO);

b) Only a Senior Citizen's Chapter Organization with a track record of at least three (3) years prior to the date of nomination and selection procedure shall be allowed to make a single nomination;

c) The nominee must be a bona fide member of the nominating organization for at least one (1) year prior to his/her nomination;

d) The nominees from each of the various Senior Citizen's Organization shall be endorsed to the Sangguniang Panlungsod through the Committee on Social Services;

e) The Nomination and Selection Committee (NOMSELECT) of the Sangguniang Panlungsod shall then select three (3) nominees from and among the nominees submitted by the different Senior Citizen's Organizations;

f) Upon approval of the Sangguniang Panlungsod in a resolution, the names of the three (3) nominees shall be submitted to the City Mayor who shall then appoint the Chairperson of the Office for Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA);

