(g) Litigable Apprechension Cases refer to violations cited in the Temporary Operator's Permit ("TOP"), City Traffic Citation Tickets (CTCTs), or apprehension report which are contested by the respondent, and the determination of which cannot be resolved without a hearing in which all the parties, namely: the complainant, the respondent and/or the intervenor, or their respective authorized representatives or counsels, shall be allowed to present their evidences, under oath;

