13. Spark Ignition Engine - means an internal combustion engine in which the airfuel mixture is ignited by a spark plug e.g. gasoline.

14. Standard of Performance - means a standard for emission of pollutants which reflects the degree of emission limitation achievable through the application of the technology. The emission requirement shall take into account the cost of achieving such reduction and any non-air quality health and environment impact and energy requirement as determined by the Department through the Bureau.

