General Functions of the LGU GFPS
Pursuant to the MCW-JRR, GFPS is tasked to ensure and sustain the LGU's critical consciousness in supporting gender and development, women's empowerment and responding to gender issues. It shall take a lead role in direction-setting, advocacy, coordination, monitoring, evaluation, and technical advisory in mainstreaming GAD perspectives in the LGU's programs, projects, activities, and processes. Specifically, GFPS shall perform the following functions:

a. Lead in mainstreaming GAD perspectives in LGU policies, plans and programs. In the process, they shall ensure the assessment of the gender-responsiveness of systems, structures, policies, programs, and projects and allocate resources based on the priority needs and concerns of constituencies and employees, and the formulation of recommendations including their implementation;

b. Assist in the formulation of new policies and enhancement of existing policies such as the Women Development Code in advancing women's empowerment and gender equality;

