A Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) shall follow the following guidelines in its operation:

4.D.1. Any person or establishment who owns and operates any Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) or "Piso-Piso Internet" shall not store any pornographic material, nor allow, promote or tolerate any person from storing or downloading any pornographic material;

4.D.2. The operation of this shall be limited from 8 A.M. to 10 P.M. only;

4.D.3. The owner of the place where the COIM is placed is deemed the owner thereof;

4.D.4. Each unit of Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) placed or operated in different location shall have its own business permit and accreditation.

**SECTION 10.** Section 5 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, is hereby deleted. A new provision in section 5 shall now be read as follows:

**SECTION 5. ACCREDITATION OF INTERNET CAFE AND COIN OPERATED INTERNET MACHINE (COIM)**

5.1. Internet Cafes and Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) must be accredited by the Board;

5.2. Accreditation shall be a mandatory requirement prior to the issuance of business permit or license to operate;

5.3. Procedures for the application of accreditation in general:

5.3.1 Application with the Board;

5.3.2 Payment of accreditation fees/charges;

5.3.3 Evaluation/assessment by the board over the application which will include ocular inspection by the barangay concerned;

5.3.4 Final approval of accreditation or denial by the board;

**SECTION 11.** Section 7 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, is hereby amended to read as follows:

**SECTION 7. COMPOSITIONS OF THE BOARD**

The Board shall be composed of the following:

The CITY MAYOR or his duly authorized representative - Chairperson

The VICE MAYOR - Vice-Chairperson

--- [Page 8] ---
**MEMBERS:**

1. CHAIRPERSON, Committee on Information Technology of the City Council;

2. CHAIRPERSON, Committee on Education, Science and Technology, Arts and Culture of the City Council;

3. CHAIRPERSON, Council for the Welfare of Children (CWC) or his/her designated representative;

4. REPRESENTATIVE, President or duly accredited member Association of Internet Cafe Operators/Owners in Davao to be appointed by the City Mayor;

5. REPRESENTATIVE, Technical Education and Skills Development Authority (TESDA);

6. THE CITY LEGAL OFFICER of the City Government of Davao or his/her duly designated representative;

7. Chief of the Business Bureau;

8. REPRESENTATIVE, Non-Government Organization (NGO) identified with information technology related advocacy to be appointed by the City Mayor upon recommendation by the body;

9. REPRESENTATIVE, Barangay representative who shall be the President of the Association of Barangay Captains;

10. SECRETARIAT. The personnel who will act as Secretary of the Secretariat will be composed of four (4) employees from the Business Bureau and one (1) Legal Officer from the City Legal Office. The Secretariat shall be appointed by the accrediting board upon recommendation by the Chief of the Business Bureau and City Legal Officer, respectively.

**SECTION 12. Section 8 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, is hereby amended to read as follows:**

**SECTION 8. FUNCTIONS OF THE BOARD**

The Board shall perform the following functions:

A. Formulate policies and criteria to serve as guidelines for accreditation of Internet Cafes and Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) in the city and monitoring of other establishments offering access to internet;

B. Accredite annually Internet Cafes and Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) thirty (30) days prior to the application or renewal of business permit and after complying with all the necessary requirements as provided by the Board;

--- [Page 9] ---
Page 9 of 13
Ord. No. 0387-12

C. Conduct monitoring activities and do ocular inspections, through the Business Bureau and/or barangay concerned, in pursuance of its functions in accrediting Internet Cafés and Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) in Davao City and the barangay concerned shall issue a corresponding certificate to the duly accredited Internet Café and Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM) that have been complying with the provisions of this Ordinance;

D. Recommend to the City Mayor, through the Business Bureau, the closure and/or suspension of business permit of any Internet Café, Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and other establishments offering access to internet found violating the Ordinance;

E. Issue a citation ticket, through the Business Bureau, with the assistance of the barangay concerned for any actual or confirmed violation;

F. Initiate, through the City Legal Office, the filing of cases in violation of this Ordinance;

G. Program annually the disbursement collected subject to the approval of the Sangguniang Panlungsod;

H. Approved uniform filtering system to be applied;

I. Recommend to the Sangguniang Panlungsod for the adjustment of the accreditation and other fees. The accreditation fee shall be One Hundred Pesos ($100.00) per computer unit;

J. Issue a permit for a fee for the holding of gaming tournament by internet café. The fee shall be One Hundred Pesos (P100.00) per computer unit;

K. Coordinate with the barangay concerned by the AEC President in the creation of their respective barangay task force for the purpose of ocular inspections and monitoring activities and to report to the Board any violation of this Ordinance, without prejudice to any report made by any concerned citizen which will reach the Board;

L. Formulate guidelines and/or implementing rules and regulations for the proper implementation of some of the pertinent provisions of this Ordinance subject to the approval of the Sangguniang Panlungsod.

SECTION 13. Section 9 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, is hereby amended to read as follows:

SECTION 9. PUNISHABLE ACTS

9.A. Under this Ordinance, the following acts committed by owners or operators/managers of Internet Cafés, Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and Other Establishments Offering Access to Internet shall be deemed punishable and subject to the penalties set forth under Section 10 hereof.

9.A.1. To allow, promote, or tolerate any person with or without any consideration promise or reward, to perform or exhibit in front of a digital camera, computer video camera, camera equipped mobile phones, web cam and the like any of the following acts:

--- [Page 10] ---
Page 10 of 13
Ord. No. 0387-12

a. Actual or simulated sexual intercourse, including genital-genital, oral-genital, anal-genital, oral-anal, whether between the same persons of the same or opposite sex;
b. Bestiality or any sexual activity by a human to non-human or animals;
c. Masturbation or the manual excitation of the sexual organs, whether or not to the point of orgasm and whether or not performed alone;
d. Sadistic or masochistic practice;
e. Use of vibrator or any instrument where the genitals, breast or pubic area of any person is exhibited; and
f. Other acts intemately related or similar in nature;

9.A.2. To allow the use of internet facilities for fraud and deceit whether of sexual or business nature such as human trafficking or promotion of indecent and immoral behavior, the sourcing or accessing of depictions of nudity, graphic sex, and all other forms of lewd, obscene, pornographic pictorial presentation of material, deceit of any artistic, redeeming and social value;

9.A.3. To allow users to access pornography, or online gambling, or hacking confidential websites, other criminal activities;

9.A.4. To operate their business without business permit and/or accreditation;

9.A.5. To allow students to surf or source data/information other than those needed for study or educational purposes during prescribed class hours;

9.A.6. To allow minors access to the internet prior to the hours of 8 o'clock in the morning and beyond 10 o'clock in the evening of any given day, except when accompanied by a parent, adult family member, or guardian;

9.A.7. To sell or allow the sale or consumption of intoxicating drinks within the Internet Cafe premises;

9.A.8. Failure to install a system for monitoring and filtering or blocking access to pornographic contents;

9.A.9. To hack and/or allow hacking;

9.A.10. Failure to post a warning with the words "NO PORNOGRAPHY, NO GAMES OR PRESCRIBED SCHOOL HOURS, NO GAMELING, NO HACKING ALLOWED, AND NO MINORS ARE ALLOWED PRIOR TO 8 A.M. AND BEYOND 10 P.M." boldly printed therein in conspicuous places within and without its immediate premises; and

9.A.11. Failure to follow the other guidelines as provided under Section 4 of this Ordinance;

--- [Page 11] ---
Page 11 of 13
Ord. No. 0387-12

SECTION 14. There shall be incorporated after Section 9 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, a new section to read as follows:

SECTION 9-B. Under this Ordinance, the following acts committed by the internet users of Internet Cafe, Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and Other Establishments Offering Access to Internet shall be deemed punishable and subject to the penalties set forth under Section 9 hereof:

9.B.1 To perform or exhibit in front of a digital camera, computer video camera, camera-equipped mobile phones, web cam and the like any of the acts mentioned in Section 8 Paragraph A sub-paragraph 1, with or without consideration, promise, or reward;

9.B.2 To access pornographic sites;

9.B.3 Hacking;

9.B.4 Consumption of intoxicating drinks within the immediate premises of the Internet Cafe; and

9.B.5 To access and play gambling on line;

SECTION 15. Section 10 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, is hereby amended to read as follows:

SECTION 10. PENALTIES

Violators of this Ordinance shall be subjected and penalized according to the following rules:

10.A. Penalty for Owner, Operator/Manager of Internet Cafe, Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and other establishments offering internet services:

10.A.1 Acts falling under Sections 9.A.1, 9.A.2, and 9.A.3 shall warrant the penalty of a fine of Five Thousand Pesos [P5,000.00] or revocation, at the discretion of the Mayor, of business permit. The confiscation and forfeiture of computer units in favor of the City Government shall proceed in case of criminal prosecutions.

10.A.2 Acts falling under Section 9.A.4 shall warrant the following penalties:

a. A fine of Five Thousand Pesos [P5,000.00] for the first offense;

b. Imprisonment of Five (5) days but not more than thirty (30) days and the confiscation and forfeiture of computer units in favor of the City Government shall proceed in case of criminal prosecutions;

10.A.3 Acts falling under Section 9.A. not mentioned in the preceding subsections shall warrant the following penalties:

a. A fine of Three Thousand Pesos [P3,000.00] for the first offense and/or five (5)-days suspension of business;

b. A fine of Five Thousand Pesos [P5,000.00] for the second offense and/or two (2) weeks suspension of business operation;

--- [Page 12] ---
Page 12 of 13
Ord. No. 0387-12

c. A fine of Five Thousand Pesos (P5,000.00) and/or revocation of business permit by the City Mayor for the third offense; The confiscation and forfeiture of computer units in favor of the City Government shall proceed in case of criminal prosecutions;

SECTION 16. There shall be incorporated after Section 10 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, a new section to read as follows:

SECTION 10-B. Penalty for users of Internet Cafe, Com Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and Other Establishments Offering Access to Internet found to have violated this Ordinance:

10.B.1. Acts falling under Section 9-B shall warrant the following penalties:
a. A fine of Three Thousand Pesos (P3,000.00) for the first offense;
b. A fine of Five Thousand Pesos (P5,000.00) on the second and subsequent offenses and/or community service of not less than five (5) days but not more than thirty (30) days, at the discretion of the court;

SECTION 17. There shall be incorporated further after Section 10 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, a new section to read as follows:

SECTION 10-C. Internet Cafe and Com Operated Internet Machine (COIM) which fail to comply with the herein above guidelines shall not be granted the necessary accreditation if it already granted, it shall be canceled/renewed at the discretion of whether these establishments will be renewed by the Office of the Business Bureau.

SECTION 18. There shall be incorporated furthermore after Section 10 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, a new section to read as follows:

SECTION 10-D. The following persons/entities found to have violated this Ordinance shall pay fines to the City Treasurer's Office of Davao City:
10.D.1. The members of the Board of Directors/Trustees, owners, proprietors, operators/managers of Internet Cafe, Com Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and other establishments offering access to internet;
10.D.2. In the case of minors, the fines shall be paid by the parents or guardians;
10.D.3. Users of Internet Cafe, Com Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and other establishments offering access to internet;

SECTION 19. A new Section 11 of Ordinance No. 0227-04, as amended, is hereby added which shall read as follows:

SECTION 11. PRIORITY IN PROSECUTION - Any violation under this Ordinance if punished by any law or statute, imposes a higher penalty, such law or statute shall take priority over this Ordinance.

--- [Page 13] ---
**Page 13 of 13
Ord. No. 0387-12**

**SECTION 20. SEPARAPHLITY CLAUSE - If for any reason any Section of this Ordinance is declared unconstitutional or invalid, the other Sections or provisions hereof which are not affected thereby shall continue to be in full force and effect;**

**SECTION 21. FUNDING - Any amount needed in the implementation of this Ordinance shall be derived from the Office of the City Mayor or from any source of funds that may be made available for the purpose;**

**SECTION 22. REPEALING CLAUSE - Any ordinance, local issuances or rules inconsistent with the provisions of this Ordinance are hereby repealed or modified accordingly;**

**SECTION 23. TRANSITORILY PROVISION - After the effectiveness of this Ordinance, upon registration and/or renewal of business permit of Internet Cafe, Coin Operated Internet Machine (COIM), and Other Establishments Offering Access to internet, they shall secure separate business permit for additional line of business;**

**SECTION 24. EFFECTIVITY - This Ordinance shall take effect upon approval and publication in a newspaper of general circulation in the City of Davao,**

**ERACTED, November 6, 2012, by majority vote of all the Members of the Sangguniang Panlungsod;**

**CERTIFIED CORRECT:**

**CHARITO N. SANTOS
Secretary to the Sangguniang Panlungsod
City Government Department Head II)**

**ATTESTED:**

**LOUIE JOHN J. BONGUYAN
City Councilor
Temporary Presiding Officer**
