XII. Exemption

Registered transport service cooperatives shall be exempted from the payment of franchise, CPC fees, and other accessory fees imposed on motorcycles owned by the cooperative. Provided that the following requirements shall be complied with:

1.) Secure Business Permit,
2.) Submission of Annual Report with audited financial statement to the Cooperative Development Authority (CDA);
3.) Submission of Tax Exemption issued by the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR);
4.) Utilize a portion of the Cooperative Education and Training Fund (CETF) for cooperative education and transport operation seminar;
5.) Compliance with the provisions of RA 9520 and other guidelines and requirements on the organization and registration of transport service cooperatives;
6.) Secure Certificate of Residency issued by the Punong Barangay;
7.) Secure Certificate of Operation issued by the City Cooperative Development Office (CCDO);
8.) All other documents required by the MTH Board.

All administrative penalties, fines, and surcharges as stated in succeeding Sections 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, and 34 shall be applied in case of violation of this Ordinance. Failure of the cooperative to comply with the above stated requirements for renewal or new application shall be a valid ground for the cancellation of the CPC or franchise and shall be required to pay outstanding fees and charges including penalties, fines, and surcharges as stated.

