**SECTION 6. PENALTIES.**

1. The administrative penalties under Section 28 of Ordinance No. 0410-10, Series of 2010 or the "Tricycle For Hire Code of Davao City" shall also apply to motorcycle taxis incarar as it is not modified by this Ordinance.
2. Any person who operates or drives a motorcycle taxi without prior registration shall be fined P500.00 for each offense;
3. Any person shall be penalized with a fine of P300.00 for the first offense and an additional P100.00 for subsequent offenses for:
   a. Allowing a minor 9 years old and below as passenger;
   b. Allowing a minor more than 9 years of age but below 15 years as passengers if not accompanied by a parent or guardian;
   c. Hailing passengers outside their established routes;

These penalties shall be imposed upon the driver. In case the operators are found to have consented to the commission of the violation, the same amount of fine shall be imposed upon him. Three consecutive violations for any offense under this Ordinance for a period of two (2) months shall be a sufficient ground to revoke the operator's license.

Non-payment of the fine herein imposed for every violation within a period of one (1) week from apprehension shall also be a ground for the revocation of the operator's license.

In case of such non-payment of the administrative penalties herein provided, a criminal case shall be filed and processed against the violator. The criminal penalty shall be a fine of Two Thousand Five Hundred Pesos (P2,500.00).

