**Article III**

**DEFINITION OF TERMS**

**Section 3. Definition of Terms:** As used in this Ordinance, the following terms are defined as follows:

a. **Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome (AIDS)** - refers to a condition where a body's immune system is weakened due to HIV infection, making an individual susceptible to opportunistic infections;

b. **Anti-retroviral Treatment** - refers to the treatment that suppresses a retrovirus like HIV;

c. **Children** - refers to persons below 18 years of age or those over but unable to fully take care of themselves or protect themselves from abuse, neglect, cruelty, exploitation or discrimination because of physical or mental disability or condition;

d. **Community-based HIV Screening** - refers to a non-laboratory rapid screening procedure done outside a health facility by a trained member of a community-based organizations or groups;

e. **Compulsory HIV Testing** - refers to HIV testing imposed upon a person attended or characterized by the lack of consent, use of force or intimidation;

f. **HIV Counseling and Testing Site/Facility** - refers to DOH accredited HIV testing facility with DOH proficient Medical Technologist;

g. **Discrimination** - refers to any action taken to distinguish, exclude, restrict or show preference based on any ground such as sex, gender, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, economic status, disability, and ethnicity, whether actual or perceived, which has the purpose or effect of nullifying or impairing the recognition, enjoyment or exercise by all persons similarly situated, of all rights and freedoms;

h. **Entertainment Establishments** - are business establishments which include bars, nightclubs, beer houses, karaoke bars/sing-along pub houses and other similar establishments within Davao City;

i. **Ethics of Care** - health care providers embraces the universal values of liberty, justice, confidentiality, respect, gender equity and equality to clients;

j. **Faith-based Organization** - refers to a group of individuals united on the basis of their religious and or spiritual beliefs;

k. **Gender Identity** - refers to a person's internal and individual experience of gender that may or may not correspond with the sex assigned at birth;

l. **Health Certificate** - is a certification in writing using the prescribed form issued by the City Health Officer stating that the person applying for or renewing such certificate, is permitted by the said Officer or his/her duly authorized representative to work in an establishment. This certification is issued to the person applying for or renewing such, after passing the required physical and medical examinations, immunizations and other examinations as may be required by the City Health Officer or his duly authorized representative;

m. **HIV and AIDS Counselor** - refers to any individual trained by an institution or organization accredited by the Department of Health to conduct counseling on STI, HIV and AIDS, HIV prevention, human rights and stigma reduction;

n. **HIV and AIDS Monitoring** - refers to the documentation and analysis of the number of HIV infection and pattern of its spread;

--- [Page 4] ---
Page 4 of 13
Ord. No. 0679-19
o. HIV and AIDS Prevention and Control - refers to measures aimed at protecting non-infected persons from contracting HIV and minimizing the impact of the condition of persons living with HIV;
p. HIV and STI Counseling - refers to the provision of information on STI, HIV, and AIDS, how it is spread and how it may be prevented, risk-reduction approaches, and information on treatment, care and support for persons living with HIV, which is conducted before and after HIV testing;
q. HIV Testing - refers to any facility-based or mobile medical procedure that is conducted to determine the presence or absence of HIV in person's body;
r. Human Immunodeficiency Virus (HIV) - refers to the virus that destroys the immune system of a person which causes AIDS;
s. Indigent Clients - refers to clients that fit to the criteria and definition of the Davao City Social Services and Development Office;
t. Information Material - shall mean any written and/or printed material which educates the public;
u. Key Populations at Higher Risk of STI and HIV Exposure or 'Key Populations' - refer to those persons whose behavior make them more likely to be exposed to HIV or to transmit the virus, as determined by Philippine National AIDS Council ('PNAC);
v. Medical Confidentiality - refers to the relationship of trust and confidence created or existing between a patient or a person living with HIV and his or her attending health care providers and or any person providing services or those who have access to medical records;
w. Medical Practitioner - licensed Doctor of Medicine engaged in health work in hospitals, clinics, sanitaria, health stations, barangay health centers and the like;
x. Partner Notification - refers to the method of finding and counseling the sexual partner(s) of a person who has been diagnosed as having Sexually Transmitted Infection and HIV;
y. Peer Educator - is a trained STI, HIV and AIDS educator who is capable of influencing, motivating and developing healthy behaviors among his/her peers;
z. Person Living with HIV - refers to any individual diagnosed to be infected with HIV;
aa. Quality Healthcare - as indicated by standards set by WHO, accessibility and affordability of medical needs, ethical care, and appropriateness of provider's knowledge on STI, HIV and AIDS, sexual and reproductive health and rights, gender sensitive in their interpersonal relations with patients and adopt diagnostic treatment and follow-up procedures of health providers;
bb. Reproductive Health - it is a state of complete physical, mental, and social well-being and not merely the absence of disease and infirmity in all matters relating to the reproductive system and its functions and processes, as defined in the Cairo International Conference on Population, Development and World Health Organization and further affirmed by the United Nations and the United Nations;
cc. Reproductive Health and Wellness Center (RHWC) - it's a wellness center which purpose is to achieve universal availability and accessibility of reproductive health care and services, provides HIV related services and treatment in Davao City;
dd. Health Education, Promotion and Development Division - Conducts information, education and promotion campaign and training on Reproductive Health, STI, HIV and AIDS activities under the City Health Office;

--- [Page 5] ---
Page 5 of 13
Ord. No. 0679-19

ee. Sexual Health - implies that the sexual drive and sexual processes are accomplished in a state of complete physical, mental and social being, not merely the absence of disease or disorder;

ff. Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs) - refer to any infection that may be acquired or passed through sexual or non-sexual means;

gg. Sexual Orientation - refers to a person's sexual and emotional attraction to, or intimate and sexual relationship with, individuals of different, the same, or both sexes;

hh. Standard Precautions - are work practices required to reduce the risk of transmission of blood-borne and other pathogens from both recognized and unrecognized sources to protect the health care worker and client;

ii. Stigma - refers to the dynamic devaluation and dehumanization of an individual in the eyes of others which may be based on attributes that are arbitrarily defined by others as discreditable or unworthy and which results in discrimination when acted upon;

jj. Vulnerable Communities - refer to a group of people who are suffering from social injustice making them more susceptible to STI, HIV and AIDS;

kk. Work Place - refers to the office, premises and work site where workers are habitually employed and shall include the office or place where workers, with no fixed or definite work site, regularly report for assignment in the course of their employment;

ll. Workplace Policies - refer to the statement of provisions of work and health benefits and rights for workers/employees related to STI, HIV and AIDS.

