Section 2. Monitoring, Evaluation and Reporting. The Davao City AIDS Council shall ensure monitoring and evaluation in the implementation of plans. It shall report annually to the Office of the City Mayor, City Council, and its own members on the status of the implementation of the plan and STI, HIV and AIDS situation in Davao City.

Section 3. Localization of the Davao City STI, HIV and AIDS Plan. The Liga ng mga Barangay in coordination with City DILG and CHD-HFPOD shall assist the barangay council develop their own local HIV and AIDS Plan, including its operationalization and investment components.

ARTICLE XIII

REPRODUCTIVE HEALTH CARE AND STI, HIV AND AIDS TREATMENT SERVICES

Section 1. The City Health Office through the RHWCC shall be in the frontline in the delivery of comprehensive reproductive health services, treatment, care and support on STI, HIV and AIDS program in accordance with the National AIDS Law, related local ordinances, and policies approved by the BOCs.

Section 2. The City Health Office through the RHWCC shall provide written reports and updates on the STI, HIV and AIDS services, treatment and trends to the Davao City AIDS Council.

ARTICLE XIV

COMPOSITION, FUNCTIONS AND POWERS OF THE DAVAO CITY AIDS COUNCIL (DCAC)

Section 1. Composition of the Davao City AIDS Council. The Davao City AIDS Council shall be composed of the following:

1. City Mayor or higher duly authorized representative - Chairperson
2. City Health Officer - Co-Chair
3. SP Committee on Health - Member
4. City Social Services and Development Office - Member
5. Department of Education Davao City Division - Member
6. Chair of the Liga ng mga Barangay - Member
7. Integrated Gender and Development Division (IGGD) - Member
8. City Health Office - CIO - Member
9. City Department of the Interior and Local Government (City DILG) - Member
10. Sangguniang Kabataan - Member
11. Five (5) from the NGOs: (1) LGTB, (1) Faith-based Org., (1) PHLHV, (1) Entertainment Industry Members, and (1) Indigenous People's Representative
12. Five (5) from line-Named Agencies working on STI, HIV/AIDS prevention that shall be designated by the City Mayor as members of the council - Members

The DCAC may, from time to time, expand its membership as the need arises.

Section 2. Powers and Functions of the Council. The Davao City AIDS Council shall have the following powers and functions as Advisory, Coordinative, Lead and Monitoring and Evaluation Body and shall create working committees.

a. Advisory Group to the Sangguniang Panglungsod and the Executive Branch on policy formulation/development, program conceptualization, planning and monitoring toward the prevention and control of STI, HIV/AIDS;

b. Coordinative Body in establishing, mobilizing and strengthening linkages at the local, national and international agencies and other stakeholders involved in the STI, HIV/AIDS prevention programs;

c. Lead Group in undertaking information, education and communication campaigns on STI, HIV/AIDS prevention;

d. Monitoring Body in the implementation of RA 8504, this Ordinance and other policies approved and adopted by DCAC.

