ORDINANCE NO. 0742-21
Series of 2021

AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE PUBLIC SAFETY AND SECURITY OFFICE IN THE CITY OF DAVAO, DEFINING ITS DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS, AND APPROPRIATING FUNDS FOR THE PURPOSE

--- [Page 2] ---
Page 2 of 35
Ord. No. 0742-21
SECTION 1. TITLE -This Ordinance shall be referred to as "AN ORDINANCE CREATING THE PUBLIC SAFETY AND SECURITY OFFICE IN THE CITY OF DAVAO, DEFINING ITS DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS, AND APPROPRIATING FUNDS FOR THE PURPOSE".
SECTION 2. DECLARATION OF PRINCIPLES AND POLICIES -
A. Article 2, Section 5 of the 1987 Philippine Constitution provides that the maintenance of peace and order, the protection of life, liberty and property, and the promotion of the general welfare are essential for the enjoyment by all the people of the blessings of democracy;
B. Section 16 of Republic Act No. 7160 or the Local Government Code of 1991, mandates all local government units to ensure and maintain peace and order within their respective areas of jurisdictions, among other concerns;
C. Section 454 (c) (2) of Republic Act No. 7160, otherwise known as the Local Government Code of 1991, empowers the Sangguniang Panlungsod to create such offices as may be necessary to carry out the purposes of the City Government;
D. Section 77 of Republic Act No. 7160 states "The chief executive of every local government unit shall be responsible for human resources and development of his unit and shall take all personnel actions in accordance with the Constitutional provisions on civil service, pertinent laws, and rules and regulations thereon, including such policies, guidelines and standards as the Civil Service Commission may establish: Provided, That the local chief executive may employ emergency or casual employees or laborers paid on a daily wage or piecework basis and hired through job orders for local projects authorized by the Sangguniang Panlungsod, without need of approval and attestation by the Civil Service Commission: Provided, further, That the period of employment of emergency or casual laborers as provided in this Section shall not exceed six (6) months.";
E. Section 458 (a) (i), (ii) and (viii) of the Local Government Code of 1991 authorizes the Sangguniang Panlungsod to determine positions, powers, duties and salaries of officials and employees of the City;
F. Executive Order No. 18, Series of 2012, issued by the City Mayor of Davao created the Public Safety and Security Command Center (PSSCC), defining its functions and appropriating funds for the purpose;
G. The City Government of Davao's innovative and coordinated approach on providing protection, security, safety and risk management to its stakeholders leads to the creation of the Public Safety and Security Command Center (PSSCC) through Executive Order No. 18, Series of 2012. With effectiveness and efficiency, PSSCC monitors essential information and orchestrates effective responses to situations and trends that affect public safety, order and security of the people who live, work, study, visit, and invest in Davao City through appropriate technological solutions and highly proficient, capable and service-oriented people.

--- [Page 3] ---
**SECTION 3. DEFINITION OF TERMS AND ACRONYMS**

Republic Act No. 7160, otherwise known as the "Local Government Code of 1991," applies primarily to all local governments - provinces, cities, municipalities, and barangays in the Philippines. It also affects officials, offices, and agencies of the national government as far as their relationship with the local governments is concerned. The Code does not apply to the Autonomous Region of Muslim Mindanao (ARMM). Being an Autonomous Region, it has its own Local Government Code of 1991, Republic Act No. 7160, by the Local Government Academy and the Department of the Interior and Local Government.

Plantilla: Regular employees hold permanent positions in the government and enjoy a full employer-employee relationship. They are entitled to full benefits under the law including GSIS, PhilHealth, and Pag-Ibig fund membership; paid vacation and sick leaves; and terminal leave (Filipinknow.net).

Job Order: Refers to piece work ("pakyaw") or intermittent or emergency jobs such as clearing of debris on the roads, canals, waterways, etc., after natural/man-made disasters/occurrences and other manual/trades and crafts services such as carpentry, plumbing, electrical, and the like. These jobs are of short duration and for a specific piece of work. (Civil Service Commission)

Contract of Service: The engagement of the services of an individual, private firm, other government agency, non-governmental agency or international organization as consultant, learning service provider, or technical expert to undertake a special project or job within a specific period. It also provides that the term of contract between the agency and the individual contractor shall be for a maximum period of one year, renewable at the option of the Head of the procuring entity, but in no case shall exceed the term of the latter. (Civil Service Commission)

RA: Republic Act

EO: Executive Order

SG: Salary Grade, a number that defines the amount of monthly payment/income that a government employee receives; Salary Grade runs from 1 to 33

ICT: Information and Communications Technology

--- [Page 4] ---
Page 4 of 35
Ord. No. 0742-21
PSSCC
Public Safety and Security Command Center, created under
Executive Order No. 18, Series of 2012
PSSO
Public Safety and Security Office, proposed office in lieu of the
Ad Interim Office of the PSSCC
DBM
Department of Budget and Management
VIP
Abbreviation for Very Important Person, a person of great
influence or prestige (Merriam-Webster dictionary)
CPU
Central Processing Unit
CSC
Civil Service Commission
CCTV
Closed-circuit Television
SECTION 4. CREATION OF PUBLIC SAFETY AND SECURITY OFFICE
IN THE CITY OF DAVAO - A Public Safety and Security Office (PSSO) in the City of Davao Shall be created.
A. The PSSO shall be headed by a City Government Department Head II (Public Safety and Security Officer) with Salary Grade 26;
B. The City Government Assistant Department Head II (Assistant Public Safety and Security Officer) shall be the Assistant
Department Head with Salary Grade 24;
C. The organizational structure of the PSSO shall be composed of
the following divisions and sections:
1. Administrative Division;
2. Operations and Coordination Division;
a. Civil Security Section;
b. Public Safety and Security Operations Section;
c. Special Projects Operations Section;
3. Intelligence Coordination Division;
a. Intelligence Production Section;
b. Intelligence Dissemination Section;
4. Information System and Technology Management Division;
a. ICT Development Section;
b. ICT Management and Support Section;
5. Development and Training Division;
a. Planning and Research Section;
b. Training and Development Section;
SECTION 5. DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS OF THE PUBLIC SAFETY AND
SECURITY OFFICE (PSSO) - The Public Safety and Security Office (PSSO) shall:
A. Serve as the command, control and coordinating area during day
to day activities, crisis and combined security operations;
B. Develop, create and operate an alternate command and control
center as the need arises;
C. Develop and support effective crime prevention and crime
reduction programs based on data gathered;

--- [Page 5] ---
Page 5 of 35
Ord. No. 0742-21

D. Design, coordinate, facilitate, oversee, analyze, and evaluate the Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and the training of civilians, barangay functionaries, and LGU employees as well as the conduct of Joint Exercises between and among the Security Units, Offices, and will be part of the full deployment of the Safe City Concept;

E. Formulation, implementation, and evaluation of long-range and short-range development plans, programs, and projects through comprehensive and systematic researches, studies, and surveys on matters relating to Safety and Security;

F. Design and implement a system that allows for the information to be collected, processed, and archived by technological means for use of the office as well as to be distributed to offices, agencies, and units relevant to security deployment;

G. Design and implement projects and systems pursuing technological upgrades and the maintenance of said projects and systems with the objective of making the City a Safe City in terms of Security and Safety;

H. Analyze and evaluate the Proposed Security Plan for government and private events for the approval and issuance of a Security Clearance or Special Mayor's Permit;

I. Acquire and constantly maintain and upgrade digital systems in order to prevent data loss or breach;

J. Provide necessary support as directed to Security Units, Offices, and Local Government Agencies in the field of Information and Communication Technology relative to the implementation and maintenance of the Security, Safety, and Public Order of the City;

K. Provide a framework for collaboration, coordination, and inter-operability of all offices, agencies, and units involved in the safety, security, and crime prevention network;

L. Oversee the City-wide Surveillance System through the Public Safety and Security Operations Section;

M. Monitor events, situations, issues, and developments in the country and overseas that may affect the local safety and security situation of the City and subsequently interpreting, analyzing, and providing constant updates and exchanges of information regarding said matters to the Security Cluster in order to maximize all resources needed to address said matters;

N. Identify potential criminal, terrorism, and insurgency targets in the City in order to determine and implement the appropriate security measures to ensure the safety of lives and property;

O. Adopt and facilitate PSSO clusters comprising of law enforcement agencies, military units, public safety agencies and intelligence agencies that shall adhere to a city-wide scope and shall facilitate information exchange including its dissemination;

--- [Page 6] ---
Page 6 of 35
Ord. No. 0742-21

P. Manage the operations of Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (AUVs)/ Remotely Piloted Aircrafts (RPA's) during emergency and disaster situations and for security surveillance purposes;
Q. Manage the periodic registration of all drones and RPA's under seven (7) kilograms that are operated by private persons, establishments, non-profit organizations, non-commercial, hobbyists, recreational, and/or sports purposes, within the City, with the assistance and coordination of the Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines (CAAP): Davao City Office;
R. Plan, direct, and coordinate all administrative functions as well as the formulation of administrative policies and the enforcement of appropriate sanctions;
S. Protect City Government Properties, Natural Resources, and Infrastructure incorporating sustainable development goals;
T. Perform other functions as the City Mayor may direct;

SECTION 6. DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS OF THE ADMINISTRATIVE DIVISION - The Administrative Division shall:
A. Plan, direct, and coordinate Personnel Administration Function, Record Management Function and other related administrative function;
B. Formulate administrative policies to improve existing systems and procedures for effective and efficient delivery of services;
C. Oversee implementation of office policies and enforcement of appropriate sanctions;
D. Prepare and submit documents required by the City Government;
E. Perform other tasks as may be required pursuant to this Ordinance.

SECTION 7. DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS OF THE OPERATIONS AND COORDINATION DIVISION - The Operations and Coordination Division shall:
A. Prepare, propose plans and execute approved programs, projects and other initiatives to enhance coordination, collaboration and improved inter-operability capacities of various responders in the government and private sectors for planned events, emergency situations and disaster operations;
B. Assist in promoting and propagating the widespread use of the Incident Command System among government agencies/ offices and private establishments/ institutions/ organizations in the safety and security clusters;
C. Analyze and evaluate, together with the members of the Security and Safety Clusters, the proposed Security Plan for the approval and issuance of a Special Mayor's Permit;
D. Establish crisis management and contingency planning;

--- [Page 7] ---
**Page 7 of 35**

**Ord. No. 0742-21**

E. Develop emergency procedures and incident responses;

F. Manage and supervise the operations of the City-wide Surveillance System;

G. Maintain inter-agency coordination with the different members of the Safety and Security clusters regarding matters;

H. Coordinate with the Bantay Bukid Volunteers in monitoring the watersheds, natural resources, and rainforests of the City;

I. Provide security assistance in the monitoring of government properties, and the tribal areas in the City against encroachers and illegal settlers;

J. Monitor the structural integrity of the dikes and the coastal road and report any damages that may be caused by human or natural intervention;

K. Operate Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (AUVs)/ Remotely Piloted Aircrafts (RPAs) during emergency and disaster situations and for security surveillance purposes;

L. Manage the registration, evaluation, and release of permits for Unmanned Aerial Vehicles (AUVs)/ Remotely Piloted Aircrafts (RPAs) below seven (7) kilograms;

M. Conduct demolition operations against illegal/informal settlers who may be damaging and/or compromising the intended purpose of the dike, coastal road, the waters enclosed by the coastal road and all other similar areas;

N. Perform other tasks that may be required pursuant to this Ordinance.

**SECTION 8. DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS OF THE INTELLIGENCE COORDINATION DIVISION - The Intelligence Coordination Division shall:**

A. Monitor events, situations, issues, and developments in the country and overseas that may affect the local safety and security situation of Davao City;

B. Maintain a constant and up-to-date City risk assessment on criminality, terrorism, and emergencies;

C. Prepare the mapping of barangays, roads, vital installations and areas that are impacted by criminal and terrorist activities, government infrastructure, religious places of worship, multinational corporations, commercial establishments, vital institutions, venues that host large crowds and all other likely targets;

D. Facilitate the exchange of information and intelligence, maximizing resources towards priorities and streamlining law enforcement and martial operations in coordination with other line agencies;

E. Analyze data to identify crime trends and emerging threats and evaluate the effectiveness of crime prevention and crime reduction strategies and programs in coordination with other line agencies;

--- [Page 8] ---
Page 8 of 35
Ord. No. 0742-21
F. Facilitate a PSSO Conference Group that shall adhere to the City-wide strategy to examine information exchange including its dissemination;
G. Facilitate the formulation and implementation of an intelligence sharing system between offices, agencies, and units to the Davao City Local Government Unit;
H. Perform other tasks as may be required pursuant to this Ordinance.
SECTION 9. DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS OF THE INFORMATION SYSTEM AND TECHNOLOGY MANAGEMENT DIVISION - The Information System and Technology Management Division shall:
A. Manage all information communication technology resources in accordance to its needs and priorities which will include planning, developing, testing, implementing, monitoring, maintaining and integrating appropriate technologies and systems into identified areas that will improve the overall efficiency and effectiveness of the Center;
B. Set direction and plans for the Information and Communications Technology Infrastructure which includes establishment and enforcement of necessary frameworks, standards and procedures pertaining to the administration, management and uses of the information system;
C. Implement proper archiving procedures or database administration, necessary back up policies and redundancy mechanisms to prevent loss of computer data and information;
D. Implement the necessary electronic security measures to safeguard sensitive and critical PSSO infrastructures;
E. Implement necessary preventive maintenance and support to both hardware and software infrastructure systems for optimum performance;
F. Provide related support to all users of the infrastructure systems which will include end-user training of the implemented solutions at all levels;
G. Provide necessary consultancy services and assistance to agencies pertaining to the provision of different infrastructure systems to be implemented;
H. Develop and maintain technological linkages to other cooperating safety and security agencies.
I. Undertake forward planning and feasibility studies pertaining to the development and implementation of software solutions and other infrastructures and other line agencies that maybe linked to the command center;
J. Develop, implement and maintain software applications that respond to common needs within the command center;
K. Continuously conduct research, testing and evaluation of new related technology that may assist in the overall function of the command center.

--- [Page 9] ---
Page 9 of 35
Ord. No. 0742-21
L. Perform other tasks as may be required pursuant to this Ordinance.
SECTION 10. DUTIES AND FUNCTIONS OF THE DEVELOPMENT AND TRAINING DIVISION - The Development and Training Division shall:
A. Plan, develop, and manage all researches and training programs to ensure adequate knowledge and skills whenever safety and security mechanisms are implemented;
B. Orchestrate training of CSU personnel and Barangay Tanods in Security and Safety Operations, Emergency Preparedness and Disaster Response;
C. Design and facilitate the implementation of inter-agency training programs, joint capability exercises and rehearsals;
D. Formulate, implement, and evaluate long-range and short-range development plans, programs and projects;
E. Analyze and evaluate the effectiveness and efficiency of Security and Safety Operations, Emergency Preparedness and Disaster Response;
F. Conduct review, assessment and evaluation of PSSO policies, plans and programs as they relate to the efficient and effective administration and operation of the organization;
G. Undertake researches, studies and surveys on matters relating to Safety and Security;
H. Perform other tasks as may be required pursuant to this Ordinance.
