**ARTICLE 13
FEES AND CHARGES**

**SECTION 1. An Ambulant Vending Fee for the privilege of occupying and selling in the designated Night Market and Weekend Street Market shall be collected by the City Treasurer's Office (CTO), in accordance with the rates as imposed under the provisions of Chapter 5, Article 30 of Ordinance No. 0158-05, otherwise known as the "2005 Revenue Code of Davao City."**

**SECTION 2. The vendors shall only be allowed to occupy the allotted space upon payment of the said Ambulant Vending Fee in an amount equal to one (1) month's rent, computed in accordance with the existing rate, as provided under the immediately preceding Section. Subsequent monthly payment for such imposition shall be made on or before the fifth (5th) day of the following month.**

**SECTION 3. The City Treasurer's Office and City Mayor's Office Drainage Management Unit (CMO-DMU) shall see to it that all vendors in the Night Market and Weekend Street Market pay their tax obligation within the allowable period and prescribed manner.**

**ARTICLE 14
LIMIT OF AREA TO BE OCCUPIED**

**SECTION 1. The minimum space available to each vendor shall be one point five (1.5) meters by two (2) meters. However, the vendors on meritorious ground may request the CMO-DMU for a bigger space, but not to exceed six (6) square meters.**

**ARTICLE 15
LIGHTING FACILITIES**

**SECTION 1. Electrical lines and services shall be provided by the city government to the vendors, who shall pay a corresponding usage fee for the fixed lighting in the area amounting to Three Hundred Pesos [P300.00] per vendor per month. Said usage fee shall be collected by the City Treasurer's Office simultaneously and in the same manner of collecting the ambulant vending fee from the vendors.**

**SECTION 2. The vendor-occupants may be allowed by the CMO-DMU to install other lighting fixtures, and use small appliances not exceeding 500 watts, subject to payment based on the following schedule of electric charges as follows:**

|  | 101 - 500 watts | 51 - 100 watts | 3 - 5 watts |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| P50.00/night | 10/night | 5/night |  |

**SECTION 3. No other utility services or amenities shall be allowed to be installed by the vendor-occupants at their space in the Night Market or Weekend Street Market without the written approval of the Technical Working Group of this Project.**

--- [Page 13] ---
**Page 13 of 15
Ord. No. 089-13**

**ARTICLE 16
SECTION IN THE NIGHT AND WEEKEND STREET MARKET**

**SECTION 1.** For the purpose of order and aesthetics, the Night Market and Weekend Street Market shall be arranged in section as follows:

a) Dry Goods

    a.1 Clothing and Clothing Apparel;
    a.2 Personal accessories;
    a.3 Footwears;
    a.4 Kitchenwares;
    a.5 Groceries;
    a.6 Textiles;
    a.7 Gift Section Items;

b) Food and Drinks

    b.1 Turo-turo Food;
    b.2 Barbecue Stands;
    b.3 Softdrinks;
    b.4 Food Stalls;
    b.5 Balos;
    b.6 Breads, Biscuits and Homemade Food Products;
    b.7 Corn, and other vended agricultural produced except livestock, etc.;
    b.8 Fruit;

c) Services

    c.1 Shoe Shine;
    c.2 Massage;
    c.3 Beauty Salon;

d) Plant and Flowers;

e) Cereal Sections;

**ARTICLE 17
WEARING OF IDENTIFICATION CARD AND COLOR CODED T-SHIRTS**

**SECTION 1.** Owners/Occupants, salesboys or salesgirls, helpers and other personnel hired by the occupants must wear, at all times, an identification card duly issued by the City Government with the Health Card ID issued by the City Health Office (CHO).

**SECTION 2.** Owners/Occupants, salesboys or salesgirls, helpers and other personnel hired by the occupants must wear a colored T-shirt as per category of items sold as follows:

    a) Dry Goods - Blue;
    b) Food Drinks - White;
    c) Services - Brown;
    d) Clothing and Clothing Apparel - Red;
    e) Plant and Flowers - Green;
    f) Cereal - Yellow;

--- [Page 14] ---
**Page 14 of 15**

**Ord. No. 089-13**

**ARTICLE 18 SUBLEASING**

**SECTION 1. Subleasing is not allowed;**

**SECTION 2. The space shall not be transferred to another vendor without the written approval of the Tlangge Sa Katauhan Management Team;**

**ARTICLE 19 PENAL CLAUSE**

**SECTION 1. Violations of this Ordinance shall be subject to the following penalties as follows:**

a. Occupants operating without an approved application shall be imposed a fine of Three Hundred Pesos [P300.00] and closure;

b. Non-payment of fees within the prescribed period shall subject the occupants to eviction and closure;

c. Non-operation of the occupant for three (3) consecutive nights shall be ground for the revocation of the occupant's Night Market Permit and Weekend Street Permit;

d. Violation of Sanitary Laws:

First Offense: Fine of Three Hundred Pesos [P300.00] and mandatory seminar (City Environment Office and City Health Office)

Second Offense: Fine of Five Hundred Pesos [P500.00] and/or Five (5) days community service

Third Offense: Fine of One Thousand Pesos [P1,000.00] and/or Ten (10) days community service

Succeeding Offense: Prosecution and closure of Operation

e. A fine of P50.00 per day per person shall be imposed against the vendor or his sales staff who fails to wear an identification card or the proper T-shirt coded uniform;

f. All other acts committed in violation against the provisions of this ordinance not specifically cited above shall be sanctioned accordingly with suspension or eviction as the circumstances warrant;

**ARTICLE 20 SEPARABILITY CLAUSE**

**SECTION 1. If for any reason, or reasons, any part or provision of this Ordinance shall be held unconstitutional or invalid, other parts or provisions hereof which are not affected thereby shall continue to be in full force and effect;**

